# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CLOUD / MOBILE dev env — copy to .env.local in a fresh cloud box, fill in.
# This is the MINIMAL set for full backend access + owner admin + the AI
# intake pipeline, with NO interactive Google sign-in. Names only here;
# paste the real secret values from the store Mac's .env.local (they are
# gitignored and never committed).
#
# After filling in, verify with:   npm run check-env
# Then run the app with:           npm run cloud        (next dev, port 3002)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── REQUIRED: Supabase backend (the real project) ────────────────────────
# The first two are public (shipped to the browser). The service-role key is
# a SECRET — it lets the server read/write the catalog and the locked staff/
# cost/floor tables with no interactive login. Without it, writes need a real
# signed-in Google session, which a headless cloud box can't do.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# ── REQUIRED: AI intake pipeline ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Powers classify / analyze-and-price / description enrich / studio cleanup /
# room-placement scenes. Absent → every AI step returns "not configured".
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# ── REQUIRED: owner access with no OAuth ─────────────────────────────────
# Grants owner role for dev@local. HARD-GATED to non-production in code, so it
# can NEVER unlock a live deploy — safe in a cloud dev box, but only works
# when the app runs as `next dev` (NODE_ENV=development). `npm run cloud` does.
DEV_ADMIN_BYPASS=1

# ── RECOMMENDED: live comparable pricing ─────────────────────────────────
# Without this, comparables fall back to bundled DOOR fixtures for EVERY item
# (a vanity gets door prices), which looks real but isn't. Set it so values
# are trustworthy.
SERPAPI_KEY=

# ── OPTIONAL: opaque-item cutouts (doors/windows keep Gemini studio) ──────
# PHOTOROOM_API_KEY=
# REMOVE_BG_API_KEY=

# ── LEAVE UNSET in cloud (Mac-only / not needed) ─────────────────────────
# PRINTER_QUEUE / LABEL_ROLL / APP_BASE_URL  → USB Brother QL-800 label
#   printing; cloud can't reach it (on-screen labels still render).
# MARKETING_DELIVERABLES_DIR  → the on-disk ad-kit library lives on the Mac;
#   set only if you actually mount PRICE-LESS DELIVERABLES/ into the box.
# PUBLIC_ADMIN_ENABLED  → prod-only killswitch; irrelevant under `next dev`.
